service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // ── Helper functions (LIVE ile aynı) ──────────────────────────────────────
    function isAuth()        { return request.auth != null; }
    function isSuperAdmin()  { return isAuth() && request.auth.token.superAdmin == true; }
    function isTenant(tid)   { return isAuth() && request.auth.token.tenantId == tid; }
    // [G1] (2026-06-27) `tenantRole == null → admin` backwards-compat fallback KALDIRILDI.
    //   Önce: claim'i olmayan herkes admin sayılıyordu (permission sistemi rules düzeyinde ölüydü).
    //   Audit (scripts/backfillTenantRoles.cjs dry-run + auth.listUsers): tüm canlı tenant
    //   kullanıcıları (whitecross+herohairs, 6 kişi) doğru tenantRole claim'ine SAHİP.
    //   tenantId claim'i olup tenantRole'ü olmayan 3 user yalnız ölü/test tenant'larında
    //   (ee-kurt-barbers / the-hair-lab / the-test-lab) → canlıyı etkilemez.
    function isAdmin(tid)    { return isTenant(tid) && request.auth.token.tenantRole in ['owner', 'admin']; }
    // [E1b] (2026-07-11) tenant-scoped owner: kendi salonunun VERİSİNİ silebilir (staff/barbers/finance/settings HARİÇ)
    function isOwner(tid)    { return isTenant(tid) && request.auth.token.tenantRole == 'owner'; }
    function isStaff(tid)    { return isTenant(tid) && request.auth.token.tenantRole in ['owner', 'admin', 'staff']; }
    function isTenantAny(tid){ return isTenant(tid); }
    // [FIN-CONFIG-DATED-EV1] SENSITIVE FINANCE AUTHORITY — tenant OWNER only.
    //
    // ── THIS REVERSES A DECISION, AND THE REVERSAL IS THE POINT ────────────────
    // `FIN-CONFIG-DATED-AUTHORITY-P0` closed the real gap (any `tenantId` claim
    // could rewrite the cost base) and stopped at owner|admin, on the reasoning
    // that the rules should not be wider than the screen and that locking out
    // admins was a product decision rather than a security fix. That reasoning
    // was right about WHO decides and wrong about WHERE the line sits: the owner
    // has now decided, and the line is the owner.
    //
    // The predicate is deliberately `isOwner` and nothing else. A separate
    // owner-OR-admin helper is NOT kept "for later" — an unused widening
    // predicate in a rules file is an invitation, and the previous
    // `isFinanceManager` is removed with this change rather than left dangling.
    //
    // SUPER-ADMIN reaches these fields through the EXPLICIT `isSuperAdmin()`
    // short-circuit at the head of the `settings` match — a specific grant on a
    // named collection. The [G4] catch-all remains `allow write: if false`
    // (SEC-CATCHALL-1) and is NOT restored, here or anywhere.
    //
    // WHY THESE FIELDS. Each one changes money already reported, or changes who
    // owns what: `partnerConfig` (wage · share · isPartner · creditTo),
    // `fixedDailyRate` + `fixedDailyRateHistory` (the cost base and its
    // projection — guarded together, or the projection is the soft way in),
    // `compMigration` (a cleared marker silently re-opens a closed fallback),
    // `settlement` (zeroes company ↔ partner debt), `initialInvestment` and
    // `initialPool` (the capital split). The app's copy of this list lives in
    // `src/utils/financeConfigWrite.ts` and a test asserts the two agree.
    //
    // `tipSettings` and `ledgerFile` are deliberately NOT here. They are
    // operational, move no partner balance, and keep exactly the access the
    // current product contract already gives them. This narrows; it broadens
    // nothing.
    function ownsFinanceAuthority(tid){ return isOwner(tid); }

    // [FIN-AUTH-CLOSURE · B] Who may READ the sensitive Finance documents.
    //
    // Wider than `ownsFinanceAuthority` on purpose, and the asymmetry is the
    // decision: WRITING the cost base or the ownership split is the owner's
    // (EV1); READING it is the explicit contract for who may open the Finance
    // page at all — `Sidebar.tsx` puts `finance` in `OWNER_ONLY` and gates that
    // set on `role === 'owner' || role === 'admin'`.
    //
    // Narrowing read to the owner alone would empty the Finance page for every
    // admin who legitimately uses it, which is a product change nobody asked
    // for. Leaving it at `isTenantAny` let every barber read the wage table.
    function isFinanceReader(tid){ return isTenant(tid) && request.auth.token.tenantRole in ['owner', 'admin']; }

    // ── [A1] STAFF-START-AUTHORITY — the availabilityFrom DIRECT-WRITE gate ───
    // WHY RULES AT ALL. whitecrossbarbers.com does NOT submit through
    //   salownCreateBooking — the W1/C1 cutover that would change that is HELD
    //   (ROADMAP WCP-3) — so it writes bookings straight to Firestore
    //   (`setDoc(doc(db,'tenants/whitecross/bookings',id))`). For that channel the
    //   Functions gates do not exist and the site's own script is a CLIENT guard,
    //   not an authority. These rules are the only server-side authority there.
    // WHY ABOVE THE BRANCH, not inside the anonymous clause. Same lesson as
    //   [P0-PROMO-2] directly below: `isSuperAdmin()/isTenantAny()` short-circuit,
    //   so a guard placed inside the anonymous branch is bypassed by every
    //   authenticated client. It is hoisted, and the exemptions are expressed as
    //   "this write is not gated" rather than "this writer is trusted".
    // ADMIN SDK bypasses rules entirely and is deliberately NOT addressed here:
    //   salownCreateBooking / CreateAdminBooking / CreateWalkIn / ReassignBooking
    //   / RescheduleByToken already apply the same rule in-process.

    // A tenant-local 'YYYY-MM-DD' key that is a REAL Gregorian calendar day.
    //
    //   A1.2 shipped an approximation here: month lengths were enforced but 02-29
    //   was accepted unconditionally, because leap-year arithmetic "is not
    //   expressible in Rules". That was wrong, and the divergence it created was
    //   not acceptable either — the product predicate rejects '2027-02-29'
    //   outright while these rules would have let a booking through from 1 March
    //   onward, so the same stored value meant two different things depending on
    //   which authority you asked. "Malformed fails closed" has to mean the same
    //   thing everywhere or it is not a contract.
    //
    //   It IS expressible, in the regex rather than in arithmetic. A four-digit
    //   year CCYY is a leap year iff
    //       (YY is a non-zero multiple of 4)  OR  (YY == 00 and CC is a multiple of 4)
    //   and each of those is a plain character-class alternation:
    //       multiples of 4 in 01..99 :  [02468][48] | [13579][26] | [2468]0
    //       multiples of 4 in 00..99 :  [02468][048] | [13579][26]
    //   So 02-29 is admitted only for a year matching the leap alternation, which
    //   makes 1900 invalid, 2000 valid, 2027 invalid and 2028 valid — the real
    //   Gregorian rule, centuries included.
    //
    //   VERIFIED EXHAUSTIVELY, not by example: every (year, month, day) triple
    //   from 1583-01-01 to 2400-12-31 — 818 years x 12 x 31 — was compared against
    //   the platform calendar, with ZERO mismatches. The same corpus runs in
    //   scripts/testAvailabilityRules.py so a future edit to this pattern cannot
    //   quietly re-approximate it.
    function a1IsDateKey(m, k) {
      return k in m && m[k] is string && m[k].matches(
        '^([0-9]{4}-((0[13578]|1[02])-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])|(0[469]|11)-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|30)|02-(0[1-9]|1[0-9]|2[0-8]))|([0-9]{2}([02468][48]|[13579][26]|[2468]0)|([02468][048]|[13579][26])00)-02-29)$');
    }
    function a1BarberRef(tid, bid) {
      return /databases/$(database)/documents/tenants/$(tid)/barbers/$(bid);
    }
    // Is this write one the gate can decide about at all?
    //   NO for: a missing/blank barberId; the 'no-preference' sentinel; a
    //   server-assignment placeholder; a NAME-keyed reference (walk-ins and the
    //   parsers store a lower-cased name, which resolves to no document); an
    //   absent or unparseable booking date; and any barber document that does not
    //   exist. Every one of those means "we cannot tell", and the contract is to
    //   preserve existing Any-Barber/server-assignment semantics rather than guess.
    function a1Decidable(tid, d) {
      return 'barberId' in d && d.barberId is string
        && d.barberId != '' && d.barberId != 'no-preference' && d.barberId != 'any'
        && a1IsDateKey(d, 'date')
        && exists(a1BarberRef(tid, d.barberId));
    }
    // The stored boundary, read from the barber document.
    //   absent/null/''  → ALLOW (temporary legacy policy: on the day A1 ships every
    //                     barber document is a legacy record, and failing closed
    //                     would refuse every booking on every tenant at once);
    //   malformed       → DENY (a present-but-unusable value is a corrupted claim,
    //                     not an absent one);
    //   otherwise       → inclusive: the booking date must be >= it.
    //   The barber map is passed INTO this helper rather than fetched inside it,
    //   so the whole gate costs exactly one exists() + one get(). Written the
    //   obvious way — repeating `get(...)` for each branch — a Rules Test API
    //   trace showed the same document being fetched FOUR times per create.
    //   Document accesses are capped at 10 per single-document request, and a
    //   booking create is not the place to spend four of them on one answer.
    function a1StartOk(b, dateKey) {
      return !('availabilityFrom' in b)
        || b.availabilityFrom == null
        || b.availabilityFrom == ''
        || (a1IsDateKey(b, 'availabilityFrom') && dateKey >= b.availabilityFrom);
    }
    function a1WithinWindow(tid, d) {
      return !a1Decidable(tid, d)
        || a1StartOk(get(a1BarberRef(tid, d.barberId)).data, d.date);
    }
    // An UPDATE re-runs the gate only when it moves the appointment onto a
    //   different barber or a different day. Everything else — cancelling, checking
    //   out, marking no-show, editing a note — is untouched, which is what keeps a
    //   pre-start ANOMALY cancellable instead of trapped. That is a contract, not a
    //   performance shortcut: a booking nobody can cancel is worse than the
    //   anomaly it was protecting against.
    function a1UpdateWithinWindow(tid) {
      return !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['barberId', 'date'])
        || a1WithinWindow(tid, request.resource.data);
    }

    // ── [R2c] FIN-DATED-ROTA — the ROLLOUT BOUNDARY (legacy vs canonical) ─────
    // R2b made `workingDays`/`dayHours`/`hours` client-unwritable on UPDATE for
    // everyone, everywhere, at once. That is the correct END state and it was the
    // wrong DEPLOY: on the day it publishes, NO tenant has a `staffRota` header,
    // so it would take the Team Members editor away from every salon
    // simultaneously — including `herohairs`, whose sole barber has no
    // `availabilityFrom` and therefore cannot be given a canonical `ROTA_START`
    // at all (`STAFF-START-A2`). A guard that bricks a working screen is not a
    // stricter rule, it is an outage.
    //
    // So the boundary is staged, and it is TWO conditions — both must hold for
    // the narrow legacy exception to apply. Each closes a hole the other cannot:
    //
    //   PER-TENANT   `rotaPolicy/rollout.mode == 'canonical'`. A DECLARATION,
    //                because creation has no history to look at — that is the
    //                whole bootstrap seam — and because a cutover is a release
    //                event somebody performs deliberately.
    //
    //   PER-SUBJECT  `staffRota/{barberId}` EXISTS. Not a declaration: it becomes
    //                true the moment the engine commits that person's first
    //                transaction, so it cannot drift out of step with the log —
    //                it IS the log's header. This is what makes "a canonical
    //                barber cannot fall back to a direct cache write" a property
    //                rather than a policy, with no flag to forget to set.
    //
    // WHY THE STATE IS A SUBCOLLECTION AND NOT A FEATURE FLAG. `tenants/{tid}`
    // is client-writable by any tenant admin ([P1-D] above), so a rollout flag
    // living there would be forgeable by exactly the role this constrains, and
    // adding it to [P1-D]'s super-admin-only key list would not fix it either —
    // that clause sits BELOW an `isSuperAdmin()` short-circuit. `rotaPolicy` is a
    // tenant subcollection, so the [G4] catch-all already closes `write` on it in
    // every role, and the explicit block below restates that so a future edit to
    // [G4]'s list cannot open it silently. Same treatment as `staffRota`.
    //
    // COST. One `exists()`, plus one `get()` only when a rollout document is
    // actually there, plus one `exists()` on the header — and ONLY on a write
    // that genuinely changes one of the three fields, because `affectedKeys()`
    // is evaluated first and `&&` short-circuits. An unrelated barber edit
    // (name, colour, photo, status, leave, order, `shiftChanges`) costs nothing
    // at all, exactly as it did under R2b.
    //
    // ⚠️ THE CLEANUP CONDITION IS PINNED, so the exception cannot quietly become
    // the architecture: when every active tenant is `canonical`, BOTH helpers and
    // both call sites below are DELETED, `allow create` returns to the plain role
    // disjunction with no rota clause, and the UPDATE guard returns to R2b's
    // unconditional form. That is a removal, not a rewrite.
    function rotaRolloutRef(tid) {
      return /databases/$(database)/documents/tenants/$(tid)/rotaPolicy/rollout;
    }
    // ABSENCE IS LEGACY, and that is the fail-safe direction: it is what every
    // tenant is today, and a missing or half-written document can only make the
    // boundary LOOSER — never stricter — so a bug here cannot lock a salon out of
    // its own team page. The strict half does not depend on this at all; it
    // depends on the header.
    function rotaTenantIsCanonical(tid) {
      return exists(rotaRolloutRef(tid))
        && get(rotaRolloutRef(tid)).data.get('mode', '') == 'canonical';
    }
    // The narrow, observable, removable legacy exception.
    function rotaLegacyBarberWriteAllowed(tid, bid) {
      return !rotaTenantIsCanonical(tid)
        && !exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/tenants/$(tid)/staffRota/$(bid));
    }

    // ── Tenant root doc (LIVE ile aynı) ───────────────────────────────────────
    match /tenants/{tenantId} {
      allow read:  if true;                                  // public booking siteleri okuyor
      // [DEL] (2026-07-02) delete = super-admin only sistem geneli (feedback_delete_superadmin_only).
      allow create: if isSuperAdmin() || isAdmin(tenantId);
      allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
      // [P1-D] Publication-control fields (profileStatus / profileSelfManaged / …)
      // gate whether the public site is live. Only super-admin — or the
      // salownPublishProfile / salownReviewProfile callables, which use the Admin
      // SDK and bypass rules — may change them. Tenant admins edit everything else.
      // [TR-A] `presentation` also appears here as a PUBLIC-SAFE MIRROR of
      // settings/settings.presentation — the hosted booking page cannot read the
      // settings subdoc (auth-only) but must still show the salon's own language
      // and currency. Same owner/super-admin gate as the canonical copy, so an
      // admin cannot make the public page disagree with the panel. (Presentation
      // holds no secrets, so mirroring it onto the world-readable root is safe.)
      allow update: if isSuperAdmin() || (isAdmin(tenantId)
        && !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys()
             .hasAny(['profileStatus','profileSelfManaged','profilePublishedAt','profileSubmittedAt','profileReviewNotes','profileCheckIssues'])
        && (!request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['presentation']) || isOwner(tenantId)));

      // ── Bookings (public CREATE + callable update; read artık auth-only) ─────
      match /bookings/{docId} {
        // [G2] (2026-06-24) ÖNCE: read: if true → giriş yapmamış herkes TÜM müşteri
        //   booking'lerini (ad/telefon/email/saat) okuyabiliyordu (GDPR PII dump).
        //   ŞİMDİ: yalnız super-admin veya o tenant'ın authenticated üyesi.
        //   Doğrulandı: salown-app/herohairs public hiçbir yer bookings okumuyor (busy slot
        //   salownGetBusySlots callable=Admin SDK); panel/staff authenticated → çalışır.
        //   whitecross-site 3 unauth read DENY olur ama: dup-check fails-open, grup-confirm
        //   zaten webhook'ta, Stripe-back iptal salownCleanupExpiredPending'e (15dk) düşer.
        allow read: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        // [G3] Public (unauth) create kısıtı (2026-06-24). Money-received alanları forge edilemez.
        //   Doğrulandı: ne BookingPage.jsx (salown.com/book, herohairs) ne whitecross-site/script.js
        //   create'te paidAmount/discount/tip YAZMIYOR — bunları yalnız authenticated panel checkout
        //   yazar (üstteki isTenantAny dalı, kısıttan muaf). status zaten PENDING/CONFIRMED ile sınırlı.
        //   paymentState/paymentType BİLEREK serbest: whitecross-site create'te bunları yazıyor.
        // [R1-A] (2026-07-24) Server-owned identity/linkage fields cannot be forged on an
        //   ANONYMOUS create. These seven are written ONLY by salownCreateBooking (Admin SDK,
        //   rules bypassed) or by authenticated staff surfaces — both of which take the
        //   isSuperAdmin()/isTenantAny() branches above and are unaffected by this clause.
        //   Verified: neither BookingPage's legacy direct-create (src/pages/BookingPage.tsx:739)
        //   nor whitecross-site's public create (script.js:1462 single + :1695 group) sends any
        //   of them; `note` in whitecross-site is opening-hours copy, never a booking field.
        //   `note` is forbidden publicly because it carries reserved block-time semantics
        //   ('Busy'/'Quick block' in BookingDetailPanel) — a public note could masquerade a
        //   booking as a staff block.
        //   ⚠️ This is R1 phase (a) ONLY. Anonymous direct create REMAINS ALLOWED (locked
        //   decision 18) for H1/W1 coexistence; phase (b) is gated on H1 + W1 + E1.
        // [P0-PROMO-2 2026-08-05] The snapshot ban sits ABOVE the branch on purpose.
        //   The first version of this rule put it INSIDE the anonymous clause, where
        //   isSuperAdmin()/isTenantAny() short-circuit past it — so any authenticated
        //   panel/staff/admin client could still create a booking carrying a forged
        //   `{eligible:true, multiplier:10}`, which the confirmation email would have
        //   announced and the till would have paid. Caught in release verification.
        //   NO rules-evaluated writer may carry this field. The only legitimate
        //   writer is ensureDirectBookingPromotionSnapshot through the Admin SDK,
        //   which bypasses rules entirely and therefore needs no allow path here —
        //   granting one is precisely what made it forgeable.
        // [A1] The availability boundary is evaluated for EVERY rules-evaluated
        //   writer, above the branch, for the same reason [P0-PROMO-2] is.
        allow create: if a1WithinWindow(tenantId, request.resource.data)
          && !request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['loyaltyPromotionSnapshot']) && (
          isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId) || (
          request.resource.data.status in ['PENDING', 'CONFIRMED'] &&
          // Money-received fields stay forgeable-proof on the anonymous branch.
          //   `loyaltyPromotionSnapshot` is kept here too as defence in depth; the
          //   guard hoisted above the branch is what actually binds every writer.
          !request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['paidAmount', 'discount', 'tip', 'loyaltyPromotionSnapshot']) &&
          !request.resource.data.keys().hasAny([
            'clientManualId', 'matchedBy', 'identityLinkedBy', 'identityLinkedAt',
            'clientPhoneCanonical', 'emailCanonical', 'note'
          ])
        ));
        // [P0-PROMO-2] A client may not add, change or delete the promise. affectedKeys()
        //   covers all three at once, and leaves an unrelated field update that does not
        //   touch the snapshot fully allowed — so cancel/reschedule/checkout keep working
        //   on a booking that already carries one.
        // [A1] Re-run the boundary only when the appointment moves to another
        //   barber or another day; cancellation and unrelated edits stay open.
        allow update: if a1UpdateWithinWindow(tenantId)
          && !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['loyaltyPromotionSnapshot']) && (
          isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId) || (
          resource.data.clientEmail != null &&
          resource.data.clientEmail != '' &&
          request.resource.data.clientEmail == resource.data.clientEmail &&
          request.resource.data.bookingId == resource.data.bookingId &&
          request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys()
            .hasOnly(['status', 'rescheduledTo', 'cancelledAt', 'cancelReason',
                      'date', 'time', 'startTime', 'endTime', 'rescheduledAt',
                      'barberName', 'barberId', 'updatedAt'])
          // `loyaltyPromotionSnapshot` is absent from this allow-list as well; the
          // affectedKeys() guard above the branch is the primary lock.
        ));
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);   // [DEL→E1b 2026-07-11] owner kendi tenant'ında silebilir
      }

      // ── Public-readable collections (LIVE ile aynı) ─────────────────────────
      match /services/{docId} {
        allow read:  if true;
        allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);   // [DEL→E1b 2026-07-11]
      }
      match /serviceCategories/{docId} {
        allow read:  if true;
        allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);   // [DEL→E1b 2026-07-11]
      }
      // ── [R2b] FIN-DATED-ROTA — the legacy rota CACHE fields are server-owned ──
      // `workingDays`, `dayHours` and `hours` on a barber document are no longer a
      // SETTING anyone may edit. They are the published projection of the canonical
      // dated rota log (`staffRota/{barberId}/rotaEntries`), written only by the R2
      // engine through `salownRotaTransaction` — Admin SDK, rules bypassed.
      //
      // WHY. An undated `workingDays` array re-prices every closed month
      // (INCIDENTS 2026-08-12): change it today and every historical wage
      // calculation that reads it silently answers differently. The engine exists
      // to make that unrepresentable; leaving the field directly writable would
      // leave the mechanism armed beside the fix.
      //
      // THE GUARD IS HOISTED ABOVE THE BRANCH, and that is load-bearing — the
      // [P0-PROMO-2] lesson, and the [A1] one. `isSuperAdmin()`/`isTenantAny()`
      // short-circuit, so a guard written INSIDE the role disjunction is bypassed
      // by every authenticated client and constrains nobody. Written this way it
      // binds every rules-evaluated writer, and the role check decides only whether
      // the REST of the update is allowed.
      //
      // `affectedKeys()` means an update that rewrites an identical value is not
      // touched: editing a name, colour, photo, status, leave or order still works
      // exactly as before. Only a real CHANGE to one of the three is refused.
      //
      // ✅ [R2c] (2026-08-17) THE CREATE EXEMPTION IS NOW BOUNDED, NOT BLANKET.
      // R2b left `create` wide open and recorded why: adding a team member was one
      // browser `setDoc(..., {merge:true})` that wrote the initial week in the
      // same call that created the document, and `ROTA_START` needs a subject that
      // exists. Denying create would have broken new-team-member creation
      // outright.
      //
      // R2c closes that seam properly rather than by exception.
      // `salownProvisionTeamMember` commits the profile document AND the first
      // canonical `ROTA_START` in ONE Firestore transaction — the engine grew a
      // server-only `provisioningSubject` dep so it can judge a subject that does
      // not exist yet, and the callable co-commits that subject through
      // `attachExtraWrite`. There is no longer any need for a browser to create a
      // barber, so on a CANONICAL tenant it may not: `create` is server-only,
      // which is what stops a cutover salon minting fresh cache-without-log
      // records the moment it is cut over.
      //
      // On a LEGACY tenant create stays open, because that tenant has not been
      // migrated and its Team Members editor must keep working. That is the same
      // narrow exception the UPDATE branch carries, it is removed by the same
      // cleanup condition, and until then a legacy tenant's new members SHOULD
      // still be provisioned through the callable — both admin UIs do — so the
      // exemption is a floor, not the path.
      //
      // ✅ RESIDUE CLOSED [SEC-CATCHALL-1] (2026-08-16). This guard used to be
      // bypassed by a browser super-admin through the root
      // `match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if isSuperAdmin(); }`, which
      // ORed across every match and could not be taken away from inside a
      // collection. That grant's `write` is gone (see the block at the foot of
      // this file), so the guard now binds EVERY rules-evaluated writer without
      // exception. The attribution is proven both ways in
      // `test/rules/staffRota.emulator.test.js` §5 and
      // `test/rules/superAdminCatchall.emulator.test.js`: super-admin is denied
      // here, and restoring the root `write` makes the same write succeed again.
      match /barbers/{docId} {
        allow read:  if true;
        // [R2c] Both rota clauses are HOISTED above the role disjunction, for the
        // reason the R2b note above gives: `isSuperAdmin()`/`isTenantAny()`
        // short-circuit, so a guard written INSIDE the disjunction is bypassed by
        // every authenticated client and constrains nobody. Written this way they
        // bind every rules-evaluated writer — browser super-admin included — and
        // the role check decides only whether the rest of the write is allowed.
        //
        // [ROTA-SSOT-2] `shiftChanges` joins them, and it is guarded DIFFERENTLY
        // from the other three, deliberately:
        //
        //   the three CACHE fields keep the staged `rotaLegacyBarberWriteAllowed`
        //     exception, because a legacy tenant's Team Members editor still
        //     writes a weekly pattern directly and taking that away before the
        //     cutover would brick a working screen;
        //
        //   `shiftChanges` has NO exception, in any role, on any tenant. There is
        //     nothing to stage: the day this publishes, BOTH browser writers have
        //     already moved to `salownRotaTransaction` (Team Members quick
        //     actions and Settings → Members), and that callable works for a
        //     legacy tenant exactly as it does for a canonical one — it appends a
        //     dated `ROTA_OVERRIDE` and projects the result back into this map
        //     with the Admin SDK. A staged exception here would leave the exact
        //     mechanism this item exists to remove armed beside the fix.
        //
        // WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN THE OTHER THREE. `workingDays` is a weekly
        // pattern; `shiftChanges[dk]` is a single dated key that outranks leave
        // AND the pattern in `financeWages.accruesWageOnDay`. One row typed into
        // it adds or removes a paid day in a month that has already been priced,
        // immediately, with no record of who did it.
        //
        // `affectedKeys()` means an update that leaves the map untouched is not
        // affected at all: a name, colour, photo, status, leave, order or service
        // edit still works exactly as before, and so does a write that re-sends
        // an identical map.
        allow create: if !rotaTenantIsCanonical(tenantId)
          // [ROTA-SSOT-2] A NEW barber may not be born carrying overrides. The
          // create path is already server-only on a canonical tenant; on a legacy
          // one this stops the map being seeded past the update guard. An absent
          // key and an empty map are both fine — neither is an override.
          && request.resource.data.get('shiftChanges', {}).keys().size() == 0
          && (isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId));
        allow update: if (!request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys()
                            .hasAny(['workingDays', 'dayHours', 'hours'])
                          || rotaLegacyBarberWriteAllowed(tenantId, docId))
          && !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['shiftChanges'])
          && (isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId));
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);   // [E1b+ 2026-07-11] owner kendi ekibini silebilir (UI'da güçlü onay ŞART)
      }

      // ── [R2c] FIN-DATED-ROTA — the rollout state is SERVER-OWNED ─────────────
      // `tenants/{tid}/rotaPolicy/rollout` declares whether this tenant's rota is
      // canonical. It is written ONLY by `salownRotaBootstrapTenant` (the guarded
      // cutover) and by `provisionTenant` / `approveApplication` (the explicit
      // bounded-legacy stamp at tenant birth) — all Admin SDK, rules bypassed.
      //
      // A client that could write it could take itself OUT of canonical mode and
      // then write the three cache fields directly, which would make the whole
      // boundary above advisory. So no browser client may create, update or
      // delete it, in any role, super-admin included.
      //
      // Like the `staffRota` block below, this is currently a RESTATEMENT of what
      // the [G4] catch-all already does (`allow write: if false`), and it is
      // written out anyway: the day somebody adds `rotaPolicy` to the explicit
      // [G4] list to fix an unrelated read, the grant would appear silently.
      // Naming the collection makes that a deliberate act.
      //
      // READ stays open to the tenant's own members — both admin surfaces must
      // show which mode they are in, and the document carries a mode, a date, a
      // reason and an acting uid. No secrets, no money, no rota content.
      match /rotaPolicy/{docId} {
        allow read:  if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow create, update, delete: if false;
      }

      // ── [R2b] FIN-DATED-ROTA — the canonical rota is SERVER-OWNED ────────────
      // `tenants/{tid}/staffRota/{barberId}` is the header and
      // `…/rotaEntries/{entryId}` is the APPEND-ONLY log. Every write goes through
      // the R2 engine (`functions/src/staff/rotaWriter.ts`) via the
      // `salownRotaTransaction` callable, which uses the Admin SDK and bypasses
      // rules; no browser client may create, update or delete either, in any role.
      //
      // The log is append-only in the engine (`tx.create`, never `set`). That is a
      // property of the WRITER, so this block adds the other half: a client cannot
      // edit or delete a committed entry either. A history that can be rewritten is
      // not a history.
      //
      // READ stays open to the tenant's own authenticated members — a client must
      // read the header to compose `expectedRevision` and `expectedEntriesHash`,
      // which is what makes the optimistic-concurrency contract usable at all. The
      // documents carry days, dates, lanes and decisions and nothing financial.
      //
      // This block is currently a RESTATEMENT of what the [G4] catch-all already
      // does (`allow write: if false`), and it is written out anyway: the catch-all
      // closes writes for every collection nobody listed, so the day somebody adds
      // `staffRota` to the explicit [G4] list to fix an unrelated read, the grant
      // would appear silently. Naming the collection makes that a deliberate act.
      //
      // ✅ Same `SEC-CATCHALL-1` residue as above, and closed the same way
      // (2026-08-16): the root catch-all no longer grants write, so "no browser
      // client may create, update or delete either, in any role" is now literally
      // true — super-admin included — rather than true of every role but one.
      match /staffRota/{barberId} {
        allow read:  if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow create, update, delete: if false;
        match /rotaEntries/{entryId} {
          allow read:  if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
          allow create, update, delete: if false;
        }
      }
      // [S1 2026-07-15] Staff comp (STAFF_MANAGEMENT_DESIGN §1.3): finansal veri —
      //   owner + super-admin DIŞINDA kimse okuyamaz/yazamaz (Finance gate ile tutarlı).
      //   Doc id = barber doc id. Comp verisi world-readable barbers'a ASLA yazılmaz.
      //   ⚠️ OR-semantiği: bu blok tek başına yetmez — aşağıdaki [G4] catch-all READ'i
      //   staffComp'u DIŞLAYACAK şekilde daraltıldı; ikisi birlikte deploy edilmeli.
      match /staffComp/{barberId} {
        allow read, write: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);
      }
      // [FIN-PERIOD-CLOSE-B 2026-08-18] CLOSED FINANCE PERIODS — the stored
      //   months. Doc id = `YYYY-MM`, tenant-local.
      //
      // WHY IT IS NOT WRITABLE BY ANYONE HERE. A closed month is the figure a
      //   settlement gets signed against, and the whole item exists because a
      //   historical total that anybody can move is not a record. The ONLY
      //   writer is `salownCloseFinancePeriod` through the Admin SDK, which
      //   bypasses rules — so `write: false` is not a restriction on the
      //   product, it IS the product. Super-admin is denied here too, and that
      //   is deliberate: `SEC-CATCHALL-1` removed the global browser write
      //   grant precisely so a clause like this could mean what it says.
      //   Reopening, deleting or editing a base snapshot has no path at all —
      //   not in the rules, and not in the callable.
      //
      // WHY READ IS NARROWER THAN THE TENANT. The document carries
      //   `operating.wagesByStaffId` — a wage table, keyed by person. Under the
      //   [G4] catch-all alone every authenticated barber would read it, which
      //   is exactly the leak `FIN-AUTH-CLOSURE · B` closed for
      //   `settings/finance_config`. So the catch-all EXCLUDES this collection
      //   (see the two `[G4]` matches below — this block and that exclusion
      //   must be deployed together, or the OR-semantics re-open it) and the
      //   audience is the one the Finance page already has:
      //   `isFinanceReader` = owner|admin, plus super-admin.
      match /financePeriods/{periodKey} {
        allow read:  if isSuperAdmin() || isFinanceReader(tenantId);
        allow create, update, delete: if false;
      }
      // A closed month is ONE document: the corrections are an append-only
      //   ARRAY on it, not a subcollection, so nothing legitimate lives below
      //   this path. Denied to everyone rather than left to the catch-all, so
      //   that adding a subcollection later is a deliberate act with its own
      //   audience decision — and so a reader who invents a path finds nothing
      //   rather than inheriting the parent's grant by accident.
      //   ⚠️ A browser SUPER-ADMIN still READS here, and not because of this
      //   clause: `SEC-CATCHALL-1` deliberately retained the root wildcard's
      //   super-admin READ grant (see the block at the foot of this file) while
      //   removing its write grant, and a root grant ORs past everything below
      //   it. WRITE is refused for super-admin too, which is the half that
      //   matters here. `test/rules/financePeriods.emulator.test.js` §4a asserts
      //   both halves so the distinction cannot quietly change.
      //   (Deliberately NOT quoting that clause verbatim: `ops/rules-authority.test.js`
      //   mutates the FIRST textual occurrence of it to prove the guard bites,
      //   and a comment carrying a copy would absorb the mutation and silently
      //   make that negative control vacuous.)
      match /financePeriods/{periodKey}/{sub=**} {
        allow read, write: if false;
      }
      match /gallery/{docId} {
        allow read:  if true;
        allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);   // [DEL→E1b 2026-07-11]
      }
      match /announcements/{docId} {
        allow read:  if true;
        allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);   // [DEL→E1b 2026-07-11]
      }
      match /public/{doc} {
        allow read:  if true;
        allow write: if false;
      }
      // Email engagement (opened/clicked/blocked/unsub) — written only by the Brevo
      // webhook (Admin SDK, bypasses rules). Staff read for the marketing funnel.
      match /emailEvents/{emailKey} {
        allow read:  if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow write: if false;
      }
      // Explicit opt-out list — written only by salownEmailOptOut (Admin SDK) for contacts
      // with no matching client doc (e.g. walk-ins who click unsubscribe). Staff READ so the
      // campaign audience list can suppress them too (list must match the server send guard).
      match /emailOptOuts/{email} {
        allow read:  if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow write: if false;
      }
      // Discount codes — NOT world-readable (codes stay semi-private; online checkout
      // validates server-side via Admin SDK). Staff read+update (in-salon validate +
      // usedCount increment); manage/create = tenant; delete = super-admin.
      match /discountCodes/{codeId} {
        allow read:  if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId);   // [E1b 2026-07-11]
        match /redemptions/{rid} {
          allow read:   if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
          allow create: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);   // in-salon staff + server (Admin SDK)
          allow update, delete: if isSuperAdmin();
        }
      }

      // ── Staff doc (LIVE ile aynı) ───────────────────────────────────────────
      match /staff/{uid} {
        allow read: if isAuth() && (
          request.auth.uid == uid ||
          isSuperAdmin() ||
          isTenantAny(tenantId)
        );
        // [DEL] (2026-07-02) staff EKLEME/ROL/İZİN ataması + silme = yalnız super-admin.
        //   Önce admin de yazabiliyordu (kendi staff'ını yönetir). Kullanıcı kararı: atama da
        //   super-admin only. Staff-doc'a yalnız Settings UI yazıyor (login/onboarding otomatik yazmaz).
        //   ⚠️ Sonuç: super-admin OLMAYAN owner'lar (herohairs durvezek@/alex2@) kendi staff'ını
        //   yönetemez — pilot kararı (Seçenek a); scale'de owner'a tenant-scoped yetki gerekir.
        allow create, update, delete: if isSuperAdmin();
      }

      // ── Parser tombstones (LIVE ile aynı) ───────────────────────────────────
      match /parserTombstones/{docId} {
        allow create: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow read:   if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId);
        allow update, delete: if isSuperAdmin();
      }

      // [G4] (2026-06-27) Tenant üyesinin YAZDIĞI koleksiyonlar — explicit, recursive.
      //   ÖNCE: tek catch-all {document=**} write: isTenantAny → daha spesifik TÜM kuralları
      //     eziyordu (Firestore OR'lar, en geniş kazanır): staff kendi permissions'ını yazıp
      //     self-escalate edebiliyordu, P1-D profil koruması + bookings delete admin-gate ölüydü.
      //   ŞİMDİ: yazılan her koleksiyon tek tek listelendi (isTenantAny), catch-all WRITE kapatıldı.
      //     Böylece staff/{uid} (admin-only) + tenant-root (P1-D) + bookings delete gerçekten bağlar.
      //   Liste 3 kod tabanı taranarak çıkarıldı (salown-app/src + whitecross-site + barber-panel,
      //     template + ${TENANT} + virgül path stilleri). functions/ Admin SDK = rules bypass (dahil değil).
      //   Storage (logo/cover/barbers/*/photo) Firestore değil → hariç. emailOptOuts/config = functions/read.
      //   ⚠️ YENİ bir client-yazma koleksiyonu eklenince buraya da satır eklenmeli (yoksa write DENY).
      match /clients/{document=**}                { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId); } // + clients/{id}/campaignsSent
      // [TR-A] (2026-07-31) `presentation` (language/locale/currency/timezone/
      //   timeFormat/countryCode) is OWNER-or-super-admin only. Everything else on
      //   the settings docs keeps its existing isTenantAny() write, so no current
      //   behaviour changes — the clause only bites when the diff TOUCHES
      //   `presentation`. Rationale: regional settings decide the salon's CURRENCY
      //   and its calendar day; a stylist flipping GBP→TRY is a commercial
      //   accident, not a preference. The Settings tab is hidden for non-owners,
      //   but hiding a control is not a control — this is.
      //   Note the create branch is deliberately looser than update: on create
      //   there is no `resource.data` to diff against, so it checks the incoming
      //   keys instead.
      // [TR-B] (2026-07-31) `packageSettings` joins `presentation` as OWNER-or-
      //   super-admin only, for the same class of reason and by the same
      //   mechanism (one added key in the existing hasAny() list — no new match
      //   block, no change to any other field's write rule).
      //   Rationale: these switches decide WHO MAY MOVE MONEY —
      //   staffMayRecordPayments / staffMayAdjustPayments /
      //   requireApprovalForWriteOff. A stylist who could edit them could grant
      //   themselves the right to record refunds, so leaving this to the UI
      //   would make the permission model advisory. The Settings tab is already
      //   owner-gated, and salownSavePackageSettings re-checks the role inside
      //   its transaction; this is the boundary that holds when neither runs.
      // [TR-D1 Phase 3] (2026-08-02) `checkoutSettings` joins `presentation` and
      //   `packageSettings` as OWNER-or-super-admin only. Phase 1 shipped the
      //   contract with this gap OPEN and recorded it as an explicit follow-on:
      //   while the feature was dark and nothing wrote the field, it inherited
      //   the general isTenantAny() write, so an ADMIN could have edited it.
      //   That was acceptable only until a UI exposed the switches. It does now.
      //   Rationale: these decide WHO MAY CREATE SALON DEBT and above what
      //   amount an owner must approve it — staffMayMarkUnpaid,
      //   staffMayCreatePartialBalance, unpaid.staffLimit_m,
      //   permissions.ownerApprovalAbove_m. A stylist or an admin who could edit
      //   them could raise their own unpaid limit, which would make the whole
      //   permission model advisory. salownSaveCheckoutSettings re-checks the
      //   role against the STORED staff doc inside its transaction; this is the
      //   boundary that holds when no callable runs.
      //   Mechanism is deliberately the SAME as TR-A/TR-B: one added key in the
      //   existing hasAny() list. No new match block, no change to any other
      //   field's write rule, and the read rule is untouched — same-tenant
      //   members still read the private Settings document they already needed.
      // [FIN-CONFIG-DATED-AUTHORITY-P0 · E] `settings/finance_config` lives in
      // this collection, and `isTenantAny` is a TENANT-CLAIM check with NO ROLE
      // in it — so before this clause any account carrying the tenant's id could
      // rewrite the wage config and the fixed-cost history. `staffComp`, which
      // holds the same kind of fact, has been owner-only since S1; the two
      // authorities for "what does a day cost" were guarded a whole role apart.
      //
      // The guard is FIELD-SPECIFIC and mirrors the `presentation` /
      // `packageSettings` / `checkoutSettings` clause exactly rather than
      // inventing a second shape: everything else in `settings` keeps precisely
      // the access it has today, and nothing is broadened.
      //
      //   fixedDailyRateHistory  the canonical effective-dated cost base
      //   fixedDailyRate         its legacy projection — guarded WITH it, or the
      //                          projection becomes the soft way in
      //   partnerConfig          wage / startDate / share / isPartner / creditTo.
      //                          Finance is no longer a wage WRITER (the £/day
      //                          input is read-only and links to Team Members →
      //                          Pay), but the partner OWNERSHIP layer writes here
      //   compMigration          the partnerConfig → staffComp migration markers
      //   settlement             the Plan A/B settlement record [EV1]
      //   initialInvestment      per-partner capital paid / required [EV1]
      //   initialPool            the pool those shares are computed against [EV1]
      //
      // [FIN-CONFIG-DATED-EV1] `exit_agreement` is guarded as a WHOLE DOCUMENT
      // rather than by key. It is the signed partner exit — accruals,
      // repayments, reversal, signature — so every field of it is settlement
      // authority and no key list could describe it. The condition sits INSIDE
      // this match on purpose: rules matches are OR'd, so a separate, more
      // specific `match /settings/exit_agreement` could only ever WIDEN access,
      // never narrow it.
      // ── WHY THIS IS TWO MATCHES AND NOT ONE `{document=**}` ─────────────────
      // It was one, and `exit_agreement` could not be named inside it: the
      // wildcard of a `{x=**}` match binds a PATH, not a string, so
      // `document != 'exit_agreement'` was TRUE for every document including
      // that one and the guard silently never fired. The emulator suite caught
      // it; the comparison had looked correct.
      //
      // A more specific `match /settings/exit_agreement` cannot fix it either —
      // rules matches are OR'd, so a sibling match can only ever WIDEN access.
      // The only way to narrow is for the broad match to stop matching, so the
      // single-segment case gets its own match with a STRING `docId`, and the
      // nested case keeps the old body VERBATIM so nothing under a settings
      // sub-collection changes.
      // ── [FIN-AUTH-CLOSURE · B] SENSITIVE FINANCE READ ────────────────────────
      // A Firestore read is DOCUMENT-WIDE. No rules expression can hide a field
      // from a reader, so "staff must not see wages" can only mean "staff must
      // not read the document that holds them".
      //
      // `finance_config` holds `partnerConfig` (wages, shares, isPartner),
      // `fixedDailyRate` + `fixedDailyRateHistory`, `settlement`,
      // `initialInvestment` and `initialPool`. `exit_agreement` holds the signed
      // partner exit. Under `isTenantAny` every barber and receptionist could
      // read both.
      //
      // THE SPLIT THAT WAS NOT NEEDED, and why. A source audit enumerated every
      // consumer of `settings/finance_config`: ONE browser reader
      // (`src/pages/Finance.tsx`, on a page whose nav entry is in `OWNER_ONLY`
      // and gated `owner || admin`) and two Admin-SDK operator scripts
      // (`analyseCompPeriods.cjs`, `wageDriftAudit.cjs`) which bypass rules
      // entirely. NO staff-app reader, NO public reader, NO Cloud Functions
      // runtime reader. `SignExit` reaches the agreement only through callables.
      // So no operational field is trapped behind this guard and no document
      // split is required — narrowing the read breaks no consumer.
      //
      // Admin RETAINS read, deliberately: that is the explicit product contract
      // for who may open Finance, and EV1 already recorded it when it made these
      // documents owner-only to WRITE. Read and write are different questions and
      // are answered differently on purpose.
      //
      // Every OTHER settings document — `settings`, `integrations` — keeps
      // `isTenantAny` untouched. This narrows two documents by name.
      match /settings/{docId} {
        allow read: if isSuperAdmin()
          || (isTenantAny(tenantId)
              && (!(docId in ['finance_config', 'exit_agreement']) || isFinanceReader(tenantId)));
        allow create: if isSuperAdmin() || (isTenantAny(tenantId)
          && (!request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['presentation', 'packageSettings', 'checkoutSettings']) || isOwner(tenantId))
          && ((!request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['fixedDailyRateHistory', 'fixedDailyRate', 'partnerConfig', 'compMigration', 'settlement', 'initialInvestment', 'initialPool'])
               && docId != 'exit_agreement') || ownsFinanceAuthority(tenantId)));
        allow update: if isSuperAdmin() || (isTenantAny(tenantId)
          && (!request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['presentation', 'packageSettings', 'checkoutSettings']) || isOwner(tenantId))
          && ((!request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['fixedDailyRateHistory', 'fixedDailyRate', 'partnerConfig', 'compMigration', 'settlement', 'initialInvestment', 'initialPool'])
               && docId != 'exit_agreement') || ownsFinanceAuthority(tenantId)));
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
      }
      // Anything BELOW a settings document. No such path is written today (the
      // one `settings/staff/package` mention in the tree is a comment in a test),
      // and this exists so splitting the match above changes nothing for a path
      // that appears later — the same conditions, on the same three key sets.
      match /settings/{docId}/{sub=**} {
        allow read: if isSuperAdmin()
          || (isTenantAny(tenantId)
              && (!(docId in ['finance_config', 'exit_agreement']) || isFinanceReader(tenantId)));
        allow create: if isSuperAdmin() || (isTenantAny(tenantId)
          && (!request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['presentation', 'packageSettings', 'checkoutSettings']) || isOwner(tenantId))
          && ((!request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['fixedDailyRateHistory', 'fixedDailyRate', 'partnerConfig', 'compMigration', 'settlement', 'initialInvestment', 'initialPool'])
               && docId != 'exit_agreement') || ownsFinanceAuthority(tenantId)));
        allow update: if isSuperAdmin() || (isTenantAny(tenantId)
          && (!request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['presentation', 'packageSettings', 'checkoutSettings']) || isOwner(tenantId))
          && ((!request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys().hasAny(['fixedDailyRateHistory', 'fixedDailyRate', 'partnerConfig', 'compMigration', 'settlement', 'initialInvestment', 'initialPool'])
               && docId != 'exit_agreement') || ownsFinanceAuthority(tenantId)));
        allow delete: if isSuperAdmin();
      }
      match /campaigns/{document=**}              { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId); }
      match /notifications/{document=**}          { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /fcmTokens/{document=**}              { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /auditLogs/{document=**}              { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /products/{document=**}               { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin() || isOwner(tenantId); }
      match /team/{document=**}                   { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /finance/{document=**}                { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /finance_expenses/{document=**}       { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /finance_payments/{document=**}       { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /expenses/{document=**}               { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /advances/{document=**}               { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }
      match /investment_transactions/{document=**} { allow read, create, update: if isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId); allow delete: if isSuperAdmin(); }

      // [G4] Catch-all: READ same-tenant'a açık kalır (kaçan salt-okunur koleksiyon kırılmasın);
      //   WRITE kapalı → staff/{uid}, tenant-root, bookings yalnız kendi spesifik kurallarından yazılır.
      // [S1 2026-07-15] staffComp catch-all READ'den DIŞLANDI: rules match'leri OR'lanır,
      //   yani explicit owner-only blok tek başına admin/staff okumasını engelleyemezdi.
      //   {coll} tek segment + {document=**} (v2: sıfır+ segment) = eski kapsamla birebir,
      //   yalnız staffComp hariç. Süper-admin staffComp'u kendi bloğundan okur.
      // [FIN-AUTH-CLOSURE · B 2026-08-18] `settings/finance_config` and
      //   `settings/exit_agreement` are excluded the same way, and for exactly the
      //   reason the S1 note above gives: the narrowed `settings/{docId}` read is
      //   OR'd with this one, so without the exclusion every barber keeps reading
      //   the wage table. A read is document-wide — no expression can hide
      //   `partnerConfig` from a reader of the document that holds it.
      //   The exclusion is per DOCUMENT, so the catch-all is split into a
      //   single-segment match (where `docId` is a String and can be compared)
      //   and a nested one. `{coll}/{docId}` + `{coll}/{docId}/{sub=**}` covers
      //   exactly what `{coll}/{document=**}` covered: 1 segment and 2+ segments.
      match /{coll}/{docId} {
        allow read:  if (isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId))
                     && coll != 'staffComp'
                     && coll != 'financePeriods'
                     && !(coll == 'settings' && docId in ['finance_config', 'exit_agreement']);
        allow write: if false;
      }
      match /{coll}/{docId}/{sub=**} {
        allow read:  if (isSuperAdmin() || isTenantAny(tenantId))
                     && coll != 'staffComp'
                     && coll != 'financePeriods'
                     && !(coll == 'settings' && docId in ['finance_config', 'exit_agreement']);
        allow write: if false;
      }
    }

    // ── Super admin area (LIVE ile aynı) ──────────────────────────────────────
    match /superAdmin/{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if isSuperAdmin();
    }

    // [P1-A] GLOBAL FALLBACK — cross-tenant deliği burada kapanıyor.
    //   ÖNCE: allow read, write: if isAuth()  → giriş yapan HERKES her tenant'ın
    //         verisine erişebiliyordu (whitecross dahil). Asıl güvenlik açığı.
    //   ŞİMDİ: if isSuperAdmin()  → top-level / kapsanmayan path'lere yalnızca
    //         super-admin erişir. Tenant kullanıcıları kendi tenant'larına
    //         yukarıdaki /tenants/{tenantId} kurallarıyla erişmeye devam eder.
    //
    // ── [SEC-CATCHALL-1] (2026-08-16) THE WRITE GRANT IS GONE ────────────────
    // This block used to read `allow read, write: if isSuperAdmin();`. Firestore
    // ORs across every matching rule and this one matches EVERY path, so that
    // single `write` sat above the whole ruleset: no per-collection clause could
    // constrain a browser-authenticated super-admin, and none of them did.
    // It defeated, at minimum, `staffRota/**` server ownership [R2b], the
    // `barbers` cache-field guard [R2b], the `settings` owner-only fields
    // [TR-A/TR-B/TR-D1], the anonymous-create bans [G3/R1-A/P0-PROMO-2] and the
    // `availabilityFrom` boundary [A1] — every one of which is written as
    // "this write is not permitted" and every one of which said so in vain.
    // Three separate packages disclosed it as residue rather than closing it,
    // because it CANNOT be closed from inside a collection.
    //
    // WHY REMOVAL AND NOT A NARROWER WRITE. A scoped global write would be the
    // same defect with a shorter list: it would still OR past whatever clause it
    // happened to overlap. The grant had to stop being global, and the only way
    // for a global match to stop being a global grant is to stop granting.
    //
    // NOTHING LEGITIMATE LOST — audited, not assumed. Every browser write the
    // platform performs was enumerated from source across salown-app/src (panel
    // + staff bundle), super-admin/src, whitecross-site and salown-panel. Only
    // two top-level roots are ever written, `superAdmin/**` and `tenants/**`,
    // and BOTH are covered by explicit blocks that already carry their own
    // `isSuperAdmin()` branch — the super-admin console's own area above, and
    // every tenant collection it touches (tenant root doc, `clients`,
    // `bookings`, `settings`) in the blocks above that. So the super-admin
    // console keeps every operation it had; what it loses is the ability to
    // write collections NOBODY listed, which is precisely the bypass.
    //
    // READ IS DELIBERATELY RETAINED, and is not an oversight or symmetry.
    //   • It grants nothing the explicit blocks do not already grant: inside
    //     `/tenants/{tenantId}` the [G4] catch-all already admits super-admin
    //     read of every collection except `staffComp`, and `staffComp` admits
    //     it in its own block; `superAdmin/**` has its own read.
    //   • There is no `read: if false` and no read contract anywhere in this
    //     file for it to bypass — Rules cannot express field-level reads, so a
    //     private field is protected by living in a separate document, and each
    //     of those documents is read-gated explicitly above.
    //   • What it still buys is the [P1-A] property itself: a path nobody has
    //     listed is readable by super-admin and by NO ONE ELSE. Removing it
    //     would change no effective permission today while adding blast radius
    //     to a release whose whole purpose is the write bypass.
    // Recorded as a deliberate retention, with the read-parity control in
    // test/rules/superAdminCatchall.emulator.test.js §4 as its evidence.
    //
    // DO NOT ADD A GLOBAL WRITE BACK. A super-admin operation that needs to
    // reach a collection no rule lists is a server-authoritative operation and
    // belongs in a verified callable on the Admin SDK, which bypasses rules by
    // construction and therefore needs no grant here. Granting one is exactly
    // what made all of the above forgeable.
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read: if isSuperAdmin();
    }
  }
}
